      "source": [
        "**Write-up note (before the ID and filter cell):**\n",
        "The tract identifier is stored in three separate columns (`state`, `county`, `tract`), so I combine them into one 11-digit `tract_id` that is unique to each census tract. I also build a 5-digit `county_fips` code. I then keep only the five counties that make up the DC-area focus of this project: District of Columbia (11001), Prince George's County, MD (24033), Arlington County, VA (51013), Fairfax County, VA (51059), and Alexandria city, VA (51510)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "o5Qa0FvNTfJc",
        "outputId": "73e2fe4b-4e09-4911-bb74-7edd3221cd55"
      },
      "execution_count": 24,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Outcomes, DC area:   (750, 67)\n",
            "Covariates, DC area: (752, 40)\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# Build an 11-digit tract ID and a 5-digit county code in both files\n",
        "for df in (outcomes, covariates):\n",
        "    df[\"tract_id\"] = (df[\"state\"].astype(\"int64\") * 10**9\n",
        "                      + df[\"county\"].astype(\"int64\") * 10**6\n",
        "                      + df[\"tract\"].astype(\"int64\"))\n",
        "    df[\"county_fips\"] = df[\"state\"].astype(\"int64\") * 1000 + df[\"county\"].astype(\"int64\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Keep only the five DC-area counties\n",
        "dc_counties = [11001, 24033, 51013, 51059, 51510]\n",
        "outcomes_dc = outcomes[outcomes[\"county_fips\"].isin(dc_counties)]\n",
        "covariates_dc = covariates[covariates[\"county_fips\"].isin(dc_counties)]\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Outcomes, DC area:  \", outcomes_dc.shape)\n",
        "print(\"Covariates, DC area:\", covariates_dc.shape)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "9eJ8gl0bTfJd"
      },
      "source": [
        "**Write-up note (before the merge):**\n",
        "I use an inner join on `tract_id` because I only want tracts that appear in both files; a tract with an outcome but no characteristics (or the reverse) cannot be used for prediction. I pass `validate=\"one_to_one\"` so pandas raises an error if any tract ID were duplicated in either file. I use `merge` and not `concat` because the two files hold *different columns for the same tracts*, so I need to line rows up by tract and place the columns side by side; `concat` would just stack rows."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "uJO-8s2QTfJd",
        "outputId": "9fe4f631-8ce7-4853-cbfe-e51b3820b8d3"
      },
      "execution_count": 25,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Merged table: (747, 100)\n",
            "Outcome tracts with no match in the covariates file: 3\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# Join outcomes and characteristics on tract_id\n",
        "drop_cols = [\"state\", \"county\", \"tract\", \"cz\", \"czname\", \"county_fips\"]  # avoid duplicate columns\n",
        "merged = outcomes_dc.merge(covariates_dc.drop(columns=drop_cols),\n",
        "                           on=\"tract_id\", how=\"inner\", validate=\"one_to_one\")\n",
        "\n",
        "unmatched = set(outcomes_dc[\"tract_id\"]) - set(covariates_dc[\"tract_id\"])\n",
        "print(\"Merged table:\", merged.shape)\n",
        "print(\"Outcome tracts with no match in the covariates file:\", len(unmatched))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "sY3sWsn4TfJd"
      },
      "source": [
        "**Write-up note (after the merge):**\n",
        "The merged table has 747 tracts and 100 columns. 3 of the 750 DC-area tracts in the outcomes file had no match in the covariates file, so they were dropped by the inner join. 747 tracts is a healthy sample for the correlation and modeling work that comes later."
      ]
    },
